<description>&lt;p&gt;Gunmen attacked an immigration patrol in Niger State, killing one officer and wounding another, and also burned the officer's body. Bandits carried out a separate assault in Borgu LGA, while a Christian humanitarian worker was slain in northwest Nigeria and a Niger lawyer was jailed for a social-media post about the army. The United States added Nigeria to its blacklist for recruiting child soldiers, and Mali expanded its reserve force by 2,400 recruits, including 800 women. These incidents show a widening of violence beyond isolated attacks on security forces to include civilian targets and legal repression. The conflict produced 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimAFBVV95cUxPQmFUOXdXMWtuM2RjaU43d3M4ZVAzcHJUamZNUFRWOE1aM2JEMW5pdUpGS2NJdGFCaUpKRElIeC1ld3RmOWdzV3llN0RzRU5PdlFuc1lwUXktQUoxd3BqblpyTU94dWJQWlNYOVJnTDcwQnludHVDWUhscmNNTW1ETzBkQzlKWVJKZkN1bVBZbFNPaVRVZmlOeA?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Guardian Nigeria News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinwFBVV95cUxOLTBXZGFVWkdDQjV3ZHR3SjE4OVZRSGxyYTVnbm55Wko5WERIRUhxMlVaa1JzdElURy05eVNQekJqeGZhZWtoTWVBVHg5TlRGSWo4SlZ2WDRUb0ZMVFZxQzkxUWJVanA0UkRfcEVqYU5JMmpjWHJxQmdMZTd3RWREd3dPcllLb0ZtV0dIaHhEbWRtZDZFdGpOLU5TYkhKUDA?oc=5&quot;&gt;Sahara Reporters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqgFBVV95cUxOWlV4cGxhcmRheHctVjdESWVGZk5ZSE5aUU5feFZkaURDWDFhV3NYWEpORW5FRmZ0N1VUZGxRZnU4SkJwVnhWUS1uT3RER0l3RXFpeVJLd0ppNTBTaHBuSHpaYUNPRm81X18yd0NyVWVJZmRkUndGbmYwZnh3Nk5paGg0MUdSdGZxUFVuWF9PQ1c4aF9ZNGRYaEU1YmtnSjhETlhDeHFEYzVMUQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;TheCable&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivAFBVV95cUxNMk91V0JkNmZPTHpqUXA4ZHE3bWZGQnJmeHdsMWRqVVdvWnlTdnVDNWJWbngwLXdkWHNfMHZzNFEyeUhiQzRtMFlIdU1IRDJ4LXVONnJVOEE3R3dUMnI3d